","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--c80ca3ef-db0a-5372-968e-c17eb31a79ca","120":"instance--69989f45-927f-57be-92e5-5102fccd9f11","150":"instance--9b02c549-b183-5406-a100-249fb1868d16","180":"instance--c1d2a890-ed8d-5123-92d5-ceeaa937ee87","210":"instance--b785b7b9-02d5-5d04-be0c-0d02d4f85620","240":"instance--cde2d3fb-a23f-5188-9d7d-6c7f3cd3cebb","270":"instance--3fa59d94-25bb-5c51-af21-1a7c1fd91f66","30":"instance--fdd04191-1a03-5134-b88e-a55240471931","300":"instance--dddeb587-c160-5bdc-a385-f5d294f11e92","330":"instance--a13b6b46-2b8e-5660-b86f-03747a07fe24","60":"instance--d996db22-4d65-536a-83bf-a1db02b37136","90":"instance--258e2cac-1806-5147-8d61-a10d64a86e46"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--15","properties":[["name","Append .akiranew extension"],["description","Post-encryption, we witnessed the Linux ESXi variant appended with a novel encrypted storage file extension \u201cakiranew\u201d dropping a ransom note in each of the directories where files were encrypted with a new nomenclature, \u201cakiranew.txt\u201d."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--878d252f-de04-5857-ad0a-e8560794a9aa","120":"instance--bf65c103-2305-50be-8098-7718a8b010c5","150":"instance--348f71b8-78ee-5edf-accb-cd536c0db67d","180":"instance--e786d536-88e4-5ad4-8526-ae120c505f45","210":"instance--d3f3806c-3238-5b69-a0ca-334a1453e3dd","240":"instance--6dc42515-8e0a-5d8f-9dcb-cc6f0eb80f24","270":"instance--6a335c70-0c01-578c-9e01-614ace562750","30":"instance--c34e4c14-a710-535c-afd4-17d8ea759e88","300":"instance--60b19ce6-d4d3-5ce5-b2fe-3427fd0ea9a4","330":"instance--dea41a44-5c5a-520f-8975-25088fdd166c","60":"instance--e8f2f47b-1824-589b-af23-ab4291258936","90":"instance--67989025-38e3-56c8-b903-f474fc067511"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--16","properties":[["name","Drop akiranew ransom note"],["description","Post-encryption, we witnessed the Linux ESXi variant appended with a novel encrypted storage file extension \u201cakiranew\u201d dropping a ransom note in each of the directories where files were encrypted with a new nomenclature, \u201cakiranew.txt\u201d."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--dbfe6415-cd2c-55f2-9509-06b6668ef23a","120":"instance--79ca45e2-afd7-51fa-9574-5085c7de4c84","150":"instance--39171cfe-3bf6-5200-b6f5-e97e3b047db7","180":"instance--8cda146b-7259-56b2-b337-56038a1f52d3","210":"instance--a662f8bf-2723-58c0-a1a8-9af9497cf428","240":"instance--a9b75b15-3be0-5e64-8132-40b87e7ae405","270":"instance--31896ecd-322b-5a41-bd1e-0b7a30b9d9d1","30":"instance--60868276-2726-597d-8f57-8aa7fc9c0738","300":"instance--4f5668fa-b6ef-57cc-93da-5cd1e1727a22","330":"instance--b022a562-9020-587c-a5be-97d254cc8f11","60":"instance--cf452b0f-192e-5357-ba8c-fbae1a6e4ae0","90":"instance--012cc6fc-0a37-5e6e-b9b7-07f3bcd2d02c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--17","properties":[["name","Target /vmfs/volumes path"],["description","In the v2 version targeting ESXi hosts, by default, the encryptor targets the \u201c/vmfs/volumes/\u201d path and will navigate into subdirectories. If this path does not exist or a path is not specified, the ransomware will fail to execute."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a73f63ad-1c10-59c2-82aa-bef4ae8f64e0","120":"instance--62757838-a58e-5d41-b7e3-1ccc64e8cdbf","150":"instance--3462202b-a91d-5325-abfe-876a63049484","180":"instance--72959cd4-5e05-5d69-a145-8b6f35720646","210":"instance--d3b85082-8de6-5ffd-8abe-c9e1ec43f533","240":"instance--0a22ffab-8bbc-55b1-85ec-df74e4a120f6","270":"instance--548b3ba1-955f-5e04-b6e8-064cc259e7a6","30":"instance--6f0a37c5-db81-5459-92c1-bc8ab8cd1fd3","300":"instance--e81be898-f7c2-56a0-a705-d2aba8831f75","330":"instance--8f207ed6-cb63-551c-9a40-583fac14fe80","60":"instance--8b44546f-f8e4-5d12-b172-99f9507395eb","90":"instance--f61db455-1665-504d-85b4-5fd5d40fbcc2"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--18","properties":[["name","Drop akira_readme.txt and .akira files"],["description","In early September 2024, we identified multiple new ransomware samples written in C++, where encrypted files are given the \u201c.akira\u201d extension and a ransom note named \u201cakira_readme.txt\u201d is dropped on the device, consistent with pre-August 2023 versions of the Akira ransomware group\u2019s encryptor."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Once initial access is established, Akira operators utilize PowerShell scripts to conduct credential harvesting and privilege escalation, such as extracting Veeam backup credentials and dumping Kerberos authentication credentials."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7